SUMMARY:South Arts: Southern Circuit Tour of Independent Filmmakers | American Pachuco: The Legend of Louis Valdez
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a screening of American Pachuco: The Legend of Louis Valdez followed by a conversation with the Executive Producer\, Steve Ives. \nIn addition to executive producing American Pachuco: The Legend of Louis Valdez\, Steve is also a director\, writer\, and producer\, and the founder of our production company\, Insignia Films. \nSouthern Circuit screenings are funded in part by a grant from South Arts\, a regional arts organization\, in partnership with the National Endowment for the Arts. For more information about Southern Circuit please visit www.southarts.org/southerncircuit. \nScreening time: 1:32:00 \nFilm Synopsis: \nFrom migrant farmworker to revolutionary artist\, Luis Valdez changed American culture through El Teatro\nCampesino and landmark works like Zoot Suit and La Bamba. \nAbout the filmmaker: \nDavid Alvarado\, a Chicano documentary filmmaker\, is passionate about science\, technology\, and human\nrights. His latest film We Are As Gods follows Stewart Brand’s attempt to resurrect the wooly mammoth\nand was adapted into an eight-part podcast by Audible Originals. Alvarado’s other notable works include\nBill Nye: Science Guy\, Blood Sugar Rising\, and the BFI-nominated The Immortalists. He also produced\nand shot True Conviction. A graduate of Stanford University’s MFA in Documentary Filmmaking\, Alvarado\nco-founded Structure Films\, focusing on science and tech stories. In 2022\, he was named one of DOC\nNYC and HBO’s 40 under 40 documentary filmmakers to watch. \n  \nLimited Capacity \nRESERVE TICKETS NOW \nhttps://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/american_pachuco__the_legend_of_luis_valdez___official_trailer-240p.mp4
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/south-arts-film-talk-american-pachuco-the-legend-of-louis-valdez/
LOCATION:Asheville Art Museum\, 2 South Pack Square\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:In Conversation,South Arts Film Circuit
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/b4bde24494-poster.jpg
